tool_input.command:
cd /private/var/folders/mc/rj708cb13vv9x7hm9rptcwqc0000gn/T/p3-sotuy2qn; mkdir -p drafts review-records
cat > drafts/0002-quiz.json <<'EOF'
{
  "id": "0002",
  "objective": "O4",
  "title": "Workflows, agents and who owns the control flow",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "mcq",
      "objective": "O4",
      "stem": "What is the core difference between a workflow and an agent?",
      "options": [
        {"id": "a", "text": "A workflow never calls a language model, but an agent always does"},
        {"id": "b", "text": "A workflow cannot use any tools, but an agent is allowed to use them"},
        {"id": "c", "text": "A workflow's steps are set in code, but an agent's model picks its next step"},
        {"id": "d", "text": "A workflow needs a smaller model, but an agent needs a larger model"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "mcq",
      "objective": "O4",
      "stem": "Your code always runs three steps in order: search the manual, one model call to draft an answer, a second model call to check the draft. What is this system?",
      "options": [
        {"id": "a", "text": "A workflow, since the code fixes the order of the steps"},
        {"id": "b", "text": "An agent, since it makes more than one model call"},
        {"id": "c", "text": "An agent, since it searches the manual with a tool"},
        {"id": "d", "text": "An agent, since the model reviews its own draft"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "short",
      "objective": "O4",
      "stem": "After each result, the makerspace assistant's model chooses whether to check the calendar, ask the student a question, book, or stop. Who owns the control flow here, the code or the model?"
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "mcq",
      "objective": "O4",
      "stem": "Which makerspace task is the best fit for a fixed workflow rather than an agent?",
      "options": [
        {"id": "a", "text": "Answering any question a student asks about any machine in the shop"},
        {"id": "b", "text": "One hour before a booking, look it up, fill a template, send a reminder"},
        {"id": "c", "text": "Working out why a student's print failed when the cause is unknown"},
        {"id": "d", "text": "Planning a project that may need several machines in an unknown order"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "type": "numeric",
      "objective": "O4",
      "stem": "A fixed workflow makes exactly 3 model calls per request. An agent on the same task averages 8 calls; every call costs $0.002. How many dollars more does the agent cost over 500 requests?",
      "unit": "dollars"
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "type": "mcq",
      "objective": "O4",
      "stem": "Every booking runs the same steps: check the calendar, confirm with the student, write the booking. A teammate wants an agent \"for flexibility\"; what is your best reply?",
      "options": [
        {"id": "a", "text": "Agree, since an agent costs the same as a workflow and adapts to anything"},
        {"id": "b", "text": "Agree, since only an agent can call the calendar and booking tools"},
        {"id": "c", "text": "Disagree, since a workflow cannot make the model write the confirmation"},
        {"id": "d", "text": "Disagree, since known steps run cheaper and more predictably as a workflow"}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
EOF
cat > drafts/0002-key.json <<'EOF'
{
  "id": "0002",
  "items": [
    {"id": "q1", "answer": "c", "rationale": "In a workflow, code predefines the path; in an agent, the model directs its own steps. Using a model, tools or a bigger model does not decide it."},
    {"id": "q2", "answer": "a", "rationale": "The order is fixed in code, so it is a workflow even though it uses a tool and calls the model twice. Several model calls, tool use or self-checking do not make a system an agent."},
    {"id": "q3", "answer": "the model", "accepted": ["model", "the language model", "the LLM", "LLM", "the model owns it", "the model decides"], "rationale": "The model picks each next step and the code only runs what it asks, which is what makes this an agent."},
    {"id": "q4", "answer": "b", "rationale": "The steps are known and the same every time, so a workflow is cheaper and more predictable. The other tasks have open-ended or unpredictable steps, where an agent earns its cost."},
    {"id": "q5", "answer": 5, "tolerance": 0.05, "rationale": "The agent makes 8 - 3 = 5 extra calls per request: 5 x $0.002 = $0.01, and over 500 requests that is $5."},
    {"id": "q6", "answer": "d", "rationale": "When the steps are known, a fixed workflow is cheaper and more predictable, and an agent's flexibility goes unused. Workflows can call tools and models too."}
  ]
}
EOF
